id: pm-zno2iu
title: "GH-1019/GH-1020/GH-1021: Node 24 nightly platform regressions after PR #1016"
description: "The scheduled Node-version matrix failed on macOS, Ubuntu, and Windows at merge commit 26feeed1480955eb20be46785c4ef4210a23916c while the Node 22 and Node 25 Ubuntu controls passed. The three GitHub alerts are one cross-platform regression incident with distinct platform symptoms and established historical predecessors."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[10]: ci-regression,context-integrity,github-1019,github-1020,github-1021,macos,nightly,node24,ubuntu,windows
created_at: "2026-08-15T10:38:13.941Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-15T10:56:12.914Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "Add focused regression coverage for all five observed conditions without weakening existing ratchets: macOS privacy-safe external-path projection mismatch; Ubuntu missing-linked-path ceiling 204 greater than 195; Ubuntu health-integrity count 1 greater than 0; Windows stat-matched cache omission of the authoritative linked-test collection; and Windows caller-owned scale-benchmark timeout at 30 seconds. Fix root causes or update invalid fixtures only where the shipped contract changed intentionally; run the focused suites and the full nightly-equivalent matrix; close GitHub issues #1019, #1020, and #1021 with the PM link and exact green run evidence."
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Restore deterministic cross-platform Node 24 nightly assurance without weakening privacy, tracker-quality, cache-correctness, or timeout ratchets."
value: Scheduled compatibility evidence catches platform-specific regressions that exact-main Linux gates cannot prove.
impact: "Until resolved, the daily compatibility signal is red on all three platform jobs and can mask future regressions."
outcome: "One subsequent scheduled Node-version matrix run is green on macOS, Ubuntu, and Windows at Node 24, with focused regression tests preserving each invariant."
why_now: GitHub opened three live failure alerts from the same scheduled run; they need one canonical PM lineage before implementation so alert state and predecessor history remain traversable.
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: "GitHub Actions run 31864756573; merge commit 26feeed1480955eb20be46785c4ef4210a23916c; Node 24 scheduled matrix on macos-latest, ubuntu-latest, windows-latest"
repro_steps: "Open nightly run 31864756573. Inspect jobs 94963923783 (macOS), 94963923789 (Ubuntu), and 94963923863 (Windows). Compare with passing Node 22 and Node 25 Ubuntu jobs in the same run."
expected_result: "Every supported Node-version/platform matrix job passes from a clean checkout; privacy-safe path normalization, stat-matched collection caching, scale-benchmark ownership, and tracker quality gates remain deterministic."
actual_result: macOS expected a shared-pm/package.json suffix but received the privacy-safe <external>/<hash>/shared-pm/package.json projection; Ubuntu blocked on linked-path ceiling 204>195 and health-integrity 1>0; Windows lost an authoritative linked-test collection from the stat-matched cache and timed out the caller-owned scale-benchmark workspace test at 30 seconds.
